WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:05.600
Bottom line: Copilot Autopilot is a bounded standing role, not a chatbot.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.933
Pilot privately with one owner, scoped access, cost guardrail and review.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:16.133
The shift is from asking for an answer to assigning a standing role.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:22.633
Autopilot brings identity, memory and a workspace; leaders still own objectives and boundaries.

00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:25.867
Governance changes with the unit of delegation.

00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:31.533
Foundry is an architectural lens, not proof of identical implementation.

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:41.467
Identity anchors the standing role; the organization still bounds interactions, access and actions, with a manager accountable for the role.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:45.767
Pilot one recurring workflow with one team and owner.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:51.733
Reuse blueprint logic, but scope each instance to its own permissions and assignment.

00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:57.967
While Autopilot is private preview, require a stop condition and review before expansion.
